From 6df258aa56d672ac92369f71057b5051f8969848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tung Son Do <dosontung007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:59:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(models): add a modelPolicy that limits sessions to
 allowed, local models

modelPolicy.providers lists the only model providers a session may use;
modelPolicy.localOnly admits only models on a loopback endpoint and no
Ollama cloud model (a cloud tag, or an entry Ollama reports with
remote_host). The registry applies the policy to every catalog
projection, to discovery, to credential lookups and to request resolvers:
a blocked model is never listed, found or selected, and a request to it
fails instead of going out without a key, which a provider that allows a
missing key (ollama) would otherwise do. setModel and setModelTemporary
refuse a blocked model with a ModelPolicyError. Both settings default to
no restriction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
