 ```
 
+`modelPolicy` restricts the models a session may select and send requests to, wherever they come from (`/model`, role settings, a restored session, discovery):
+
+- `modelPolicy.providers`: the only model providers allowed. Empty (the default) allows every provider. A provider outside the list behaves as if it were in `disabledProviders`.
+- `modelPolicy.localOnly`: admit only models served from this computer: the model's endpoint must be a loopback address, and no Ollama cloud model is admitted (a tag whose name or `:tag` part is `cloud` or ends in `-cloud`, or an entry Ollama reports with `remote_host`). Default `false`.
+
+A blocked model is absent from the catalog, `setModel` refuses it, and a request to it fails instead of being sent without a key.
+
+```yaml
+modelPolicy:
+  providers: [ollama]
+  localOnly: true
+```
+
 The default is an empty array (nothing disabled). For the two subsystems' provider ids and ordering, see [Providers](./providers.md) and [Context files](./context-files.md).
 
 Native project `modelRoles` are also read directly from `.omp/config.yml`; disabling the `native` discovery provider does not suppress that model-role layer.
